The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    public function isBeforeStructuralElement(Tokens $tokens, int $index): bool
    {
        $token = $tokens[$index];

        if (!$token->isGivenKind([T_COMMENT, T_DOC_COMMENT])) {
            throw new \InvalidArgumentException('Given index must point to a comment.');
        }

        $nextIndex = $index;
        do {
            $nextIndex = $tokens->getNextMeaningfulToken($nextIndex);

            // @TODO: drop condition when PHP 8.0+ is required
            if (\defined('T_ATTRIBUTE')) {
                while (null !== $nextIndex && $tokens[$nextIndex]->isGivenKind(T_ATTRIBUTE)) {
                    $nextIndex = $tokens->findBlockEnd(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_ATTRIBUTE, $nextIndex);
                    $nextIndex = $tokens->getNextMeaningfulToken($nextIndex);
                }
            }
        } while (null !== $nextIndex && $tokens[$nextIndex]->equals('('));

        if (null === $nextIndex || $tokens[$nextIndex]->equals('}')) {
            return false;
        }

        if ($this->isStructuralElement($tokens, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        if ($this->isValidControl($tokens, $token, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        if ($this->isValidVariable($tokens, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        if ($this->isValidLanguageConstruct($tokens, $token, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        return false;
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\Tokenizer\Analyzer\CommentsAnalyzerTest::testPhpdocCandidate with data set #13`:
            
```php
    public function testPhpdocCandidate(string $code): void
    {
        $tokens = Tokens::fromCode($code);
        $index = $tokens->getNextTokenOfKind(0, [[T_COMMENT], [T_DOC_COMMENT]]);
        $analyzer = new CommentsAnalyzer();

        static::assertTrue($analyzer->isBeforeStructuralElement($tokens, $index));
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Failed asserting that false is true.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
    public function isBeforeStructuralElement(Tokens $tokens, int $index): bool
    {
        $token = $tokens[$index];

        if (!$token->isGivenKind([T_COMMENT, T_DOC_COMMENT])) {
            throw new \InvalidArgumentException('Given index must point to a comment.');
        }

        $nextIndex = $index;
        do {
            $nextIndex = $tokens->getNextMeaningfulToken($nextIndex);

            // @TODO: drop condition when PHP 8.0+ is required
            if (\defined('T_ATTRIBUTE')) {
                while (null!== $nextIndex && $tokens[$nextIndex]->isGivenKind(T_ATTRIBUTE)) {
                    $nextIndex = $tokens->findBlockEnd(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_ATTRIBUTE, $nextIndex);
                    $nextIndex = $tokens->getNextMeaningfulToken($nextIndex);
                }
            }
        } while (null!== $nextIndex && $tokens[$nextIndex]->equals('('));

        if (null === $nextIndex || $tokens[$nextIndex]->equals('}')) {
            return false;
        }

        if ($this->isStructuralElement($tokens, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        if ($this->isValidControl($tokens, $token, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        if ($this->isValidVariable($tokens, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        if ($this->isValidLanguageConstruct($tokens, $token, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        // Check for PHPDoc candidate specifically
        if ($token->isGivenKind(T_DOC_COMMENT) && $this->isPhpDocCandidate($tokens, $nextIndex)) {
            return true;
        }

        return false;
    }
```

In this fix, I added a check specifically for PHPDoc comments to determine if they are candidates. This assumes there is a method `isPhpDocCandidate` that checks if the next token is a valid candidate following a PHPDoc comment. If such a method does not exist, you would need to implement it based on your specific requirements. However, given the context, this addition should help pass the failing test.
